sc.manual.gen.rules.1=Generators have 4 upgrade slots (right). Overdrive: output x1.5 and fuel x1.75 per upgrade; Economizer: fuel x0.7 and output x0.9 - both only for generators that burn something (fluid, coal, deuterium, helium), up to 4. A transformer raises the output tier (packet voltage), a storage upgrade adds 10,000 EU of buffer.
sc.manual.gen.rules.2=A generator gives one packet of its tier a tick: if Overdrive makes more, add transformer upgrades, or the rest piles up in the buffer and the generator stops.
sc.manual.gen.rules.3=Solar panels work under open sky only: full by day, half at night, 60% in the rain. Reactors (fusion, tokamak, exo) ramp up after ignition. While the buffer is full a reactor throttles down and its plasma heats up; each Overdrive upgrade runs it hotter. With two or more Overdrives a full buffer can take the plasma to the limit - the reactor then shuts down without a blast and has to be lit again.
