sc.manual.machines.quarryhead=Silicon Quarry
sc.manual.machines.quarry.1=The LV / MV / HV / EV quarry digs its area layer by layer from its own level down: by default a square centred on it (up to 8 / 16 / 32 / 64 blocks), or an area card's box. It needs a drill head: steel (1 block/s, no obsidian), tungsten (2), diamond (4), Exo (8, never wears, energy x1.5); the quarry's tier multiplies the speed. What it digs goes into a 27-slot buffer and on into any chest or pipe next to it.
sc.manual.machines.quarry.2=Six tabs: Quarry (status, start / pause / reset, forecast, XP, redstone, power mode), Area (size, offset, bottom, shape, what's left behind, and how the area shows: always / with a wrench / in the menu, dashes, layer plane, brightness, frame and plane colours - palette or R/G/B sliders), Map (from above, ore found), Output (filter, output side, buffer), Functions (switch what the modules add; power modes) and Modules.
sc.manual.machines.quarry.3=In the world the area is a laser frame with running dashes, turning corner beacons with its size, a glowing grid on the layer being dug. The quarry won't dig in someone else's private field zone. Wrenched off or broken, it keeps its settings and progress.
